{
  "dom_id": "step-q266026",
  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14225277/assets/6d1f3a4ec50d76a52dc6a3a989d3779b529058d0de9c31d627d76a139884ff58.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the angle $\\theta =\\frac{11\\pi }{6}$ in the coordinate plane. Expressed in radians, what is its reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}?$\n\n${\\theta }_{R}\\,=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14225277/assets/4672b0e5bf7db7d8eecc659ecd988c94d7e290c426a673d82d9b3299f02dc20b.png)\n\nThe reference angle, denoted ${\\theta }_{R},$  is the angle that $\\theta $ makes with the $x$-axis.\n\nAs $\\theta $ is in the fourth quadrant, its reference angle is given by\n\n$$\n{\\theta }_{R}=2\\pi -\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\theta }_{R}=2\\pi -\\frac{11\\pi }{6}=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.\n$$",
